# Features layering doctrine (porto-features)

**Docs:** `docs/vocabulary.md` · `docs/scenario-policy.md` · `docs/matrix.md` · **PR review:** [`.cursor/BUGBOT.md`](../BUGBOT.md)

**Agent siblings:** [karpathy-guidelines.mdc](karpathy-guidelines.mdc) · [git-no-auto-commit.mdc](git-no-auto-commit.mdc)

porto-features is a **shared BDD contract** package — Gherkin scenarios and JSON fixtures only. Step definitions belong in **implementor test suites** (any language), not in this repo.

## The stack (do not collapse)

```text
porto-data (facts)     →  catalog JSON + schemas
porto-features (BDD)   →  behavior contracts (this repo)
Implementor runners    →  step definitions + execution (outside this repo)
```

Wire-derived adapter Examples and `orders.generated.yaml` are **generated** in Porto SDK Lab via `matrix-orders-sync.py` — the only Lab-specific coupling documented here.

## Core principles

1. **Implementation-agnostic Gherkin.** No Python class names, TypeScript modules, or framework internals in `.feature` files.

2. **Input vs assertion identifiers.**
   - **Given / When input:** `porto_id` size buckets (`small`, `medium`, `large`, `extra_large`) and service `porto_id` (`registered`, …).
   - **Then assertions:** native catalog `id` (`standardbrief`, `einschreiben`, …) when verifying resolution output.

3. **No step definitions here.** Never add `tests/bdd/steps/**` or runner glue in this repo.

4. **Published paths only.** `porto_features/errors.json`, features under `porto_features/features/` (including `sdk/` and `adapters/`), address fixtures under `porto_features/fixtures/`. No `contracts/` folder.

5. **Tag every Feature.** `@sdk` or `@adapters` at Feature level; `@canary` / `@heavy` on paid adapter scenarios when a smoke or expensive wire matrix is intended. **All tags lowercase** — never `@SDK`, `@Heavy`, `@Full`, or `@Release`.

6. **No fake mark simulation.** Offline resolve is `When I resolve the letter` in `sdk/providers/{operator}/resolution.feature`. Do not add `mark_simulate`, `stamp_generation`, or CLI stamp-simulate. Paid purchase is `When I create a mark` on `marks.feature`.

7. **Letter, not shipment.** Customer copy uses letter / price / mailing requirements / additional services. Do not write shipping or shipment. Eligibility is inside resolve — not `When I check restrictions`. Catalog reads are `When I inspect … data`.

**0.x:** No version pin file — keep porto-data, porto-features, and implementor packages aligned on breaking changes until `1.x`.

## Red flags

| Smell | Fix |
|-------|-----|
| `letter_standard`, `STANDARD` as product input | Use `porto_id` `small` |
| `registered_mail` as service pick | Use service `porto_id` `registered` |
| Step defs in this repo | Move to implementor test suites |
| Hand-edited `orders.generated.yaml` | Regenerate via Porto SDK Lab `matrix-orders-sync.py` |
| `@offline` / `@online` / `@api` | Use `@sdk` / `@adapters` per `docs/scenario-policy.md` |
| `@full` / `@release` | Use `@heavy` on paid adapter scenarios |
| `When I simulate stamp generation` / CLI stamp simulate | Use `resolution.feature`; paid path is `When I create a mark` |
| `shipping` / `shipment` in Gherkin | letter / price / mailing requirements |
| `When I check restrictions` / `When I access` | `When I resolve the letter` / `When I inspect … data` |
| `When I prepare a mark order` | `When I attempt to create a mark` (errors) or unit tests |
| `contracts/` or `porto_features/matrix/` | Catalog is `errors.json`; indexes live in Lab `labs/matrix/` |
| Scenario references `data_links.json` | Use `graph.json`, `execution.json`, `metadata.json` |

## Before merge

PR review blocking rules: see `.cursor/BUGBOT.md` (not duplicated here).

1. `make quality` and `make test-cov`
2. Update `docs/vocabulary.md` when adding canonical steps
3. Update `CHANGELOG.md` for behavior-spec changes
4. Validator rules in `scripts/validate_features.py` and `scripts/validate_error_contracts.py` when new patterns are introduced
